{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick feels relevant because my Raspberry Pi entertainment setup gives me a concrete reason to consider easier TV streaming.",
    "The larger SanDisk card connects to my past memory-card purchases and Raspberry Pi projects, where extra storage could help if the card is compatible."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers, smart displays and camera introduce uses I have not been pursuing; buying computer accessories does not mean I want voice control or home monitoring.",
    "The 24-port switch relates to my wired-networking purchases, but its scale exceeds my apparent needs. The HDMI cable is relevant too, yet owning one already reduces my reason to choose another now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any connected household device.",
    "My networking and memory-card purchases seem to be taken as reasons to recommend larger equipment, even though more capacity only matters when it serves a specific use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent adapter, Ethernet cables, backpack, headphone mount and duster suggest practical improvements to a computer workspace, which these recommendations barely address.",
    "The purpose and compatibility of an accessory matter to me: a card for a Garmin GPS and storage for a Raspberry Pi are different needs, and a cable I already own is not automatically a useful next purchase."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my entertainment and storage interests but miss my stronger focus on practical accessories that solve a specific setup need."
}"}
